[b]Single player only. Build 42.[/b]

A decorating cheat. Pick a room type (kitchen, bedroom, living room, dining room, bar or garage) and place its furniture and floors for free. The lists are built from the game's own tiles, so matching furniture from tile mods shows up too.

[h2]How to use[/h2]
[list]
[*]Press F7, or right-click a room and choose Furnish this kitchen... (or bedroom, and so on). It opens on the room you're standing in.
[*]Click an item, then click in the world to place it. R rotates, red means it doesn't fit. Keep clicking to place more. Right-click or Esc when done.
[*]Floors: click inside a room to floor all of it, or drag to paint a rectangle.
[*]Remove, then click a piece of furniture. Beds and couches go as one piece.
[*]Ctrl+Z or Undo takes back the last 50 changes.
[/list]

Pieces are placed with the same game code the debug tile brush uses, and their containers start empty.

[h2]Options[/h2]
Options > Mods > Room Furnisher:
[list]
[*]Open key: F7
[*]Layout: Catalog window (default: room tabs, filters, search, a picture grid) or Bottom strip (eight items along the bottom of the screen). A button in either layout switches too.
[*]Ignore placement rules: off. When on, furniture goes on any square with a floor.
[/list]

[h2]Compatibility[/h2]
Single player only. In multiplayer the mod does nothing.

[h2]Known issues[/h2]
[list]
[*]The first open reads every tile sheet and may hitch for a moment.
[*]Bed and couch cards show only one tile.
[*]Undo puts furniture back empty, doesn't restore floor blends or dirt, and is cleared when you quit.
[*]The game has no TV stand tile. Low tables are under Living room > Tables.
[*]Below about 1100 px wide, the bottom strip's buttons can overlap.
[/list]

Source and bug reports: [url=https://github.com/maxcwolf/pz-mods/tree/main/furnish-by-room]GitHub[/url]
